.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn xft_sqrt
and
.Fn xft_dsqrt
return
.Ql \-1
for a negative input on targets other than x86_64, and a NaN on x86_64.
The two backends are not interchangeable.
.Pp
.Fn xft_rsqrt
and
.Fn xft_drsqrt
are approximations everywhere and are not correctly rounded even on
x86_64.
.Pp
.Fn xft_floorf
and
.Fn xft_ceilf
cast
.Fa x
to
.Vt long long ,
so
.Fa x
must lie within the range of that type.
.Fn xft_floorf
also returns positive zero for a negative zero input, because the cast of
.Ql \-0.0f
is
.Ql 0 .
.Pp
.Fn xft_roundf
clamps
.Fa n
to 7 and its power-of-ten multiplier is initialised to 0.1 rather than
1.0, so
.Fa n
is effectively off by one for all values at or above 1.
Pass
.Fa n
+ 1 or use
.Fn xft_roundff
when rounding to an integer.
.Pp
The integer power functions do not check for overflow.
.Pp
The 3D helpers use GCC and Clang vector extensions and are not portable to
compilers without them.
